  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_18ce5200_00f5_45bb_8c6f_6fb128cd41ae">
    <emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">A reference can be a measurement unit, a measurement procedure, a reference material, or a combination of such (VIM3 1.1 NOTE 2).</emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
    <emmo:EMMO_8a137e9f_579c_4e28_baca_e8980eb0c3db rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">EquivalentTo: StandardUnit or MeasurementUnit or ProcedureUnit</emmo:EMMO_8a137e9f_579c_4e28_baca_e8980eb0c3db>
    <emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f xml:lang="en">A symbolic is recognized as reference unit also if it is not part of a quantity (e.g. as in the sentence "the Bq is the reference unit of Becquerel").
For this reason we can't declare the axiom:
MetrologicalReference SubClassOf: inverse(hasMetrologicalReference) some Quantity
because there exist reference units without being part of a quantity.
This is peculiar to EMMO, where quantities as syntatic entities (explicit quantities) are distinct with quantities as semantic entities (properties).</emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">MetrologicalReference</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_985bec21_989f_4b9e_a4b3_735d88099c3c"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">MetrologicalReference</skos:prefLabel>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reference can be a measurement unit, a measurement procedure, a reference material, or a combination of such (VIM3 1.1 NOTE 2).</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo/disciplines/isq#"/>
  </rdf:Description>
