    <emmo:EMMO_33ae2d07_5526_4555_a0b4_8f4c031b5652 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">R</emmo:EMMO_33ae2d07_5526_4555_a0b4_8f4c031b5652>
    <emmo:EMMO_7f1dec83_d85e_4e1b_b7bd_c9442d4f5a64 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">R</emmo:EMMO_7f1dec83_d85e_4e1b_b7bd_c9442d4f5a64>
    <emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">Not to be confused with roentgen equivalent man or roentgen equivalent physical. The roentgen (symbol R) is an obsolete unit of measurement for the kerma of X-rays and gamma rays up to 3 MeV.

