  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_8681074a_e225_4e38_b586_e85b0f43ce38">
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">All or part of the programs, procedures, rules, and associated documentation of an information processing system.</rdfs:comment>
    <emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">All or part of the programs, procedures, rules, and associated documentation of an information processing system.</emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Software</skos:prefLabel>
    <emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f xml:lang="en">Software is usually used as a generic term for programs. However, in its broadest sense it can refer to all information (i.e., both programs and data) in electronic form and can provide a distinction from hardware, which refers to computers or other electronic systems on which software can exist and be use.
Here we explicitly include in the definition also all the data (e.g. source code, script files) that takes part to the building of the executable, are necessary to the execution of a program or that document it for the users.</emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_4db96fb7_e9e0_466d_942b_f6f17bfdc145"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Software</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo/disciplines/models#"/>
  </rdf:Description>
