  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_704630b8_fee3_49b9_baca_40e2dd276370">
    <emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f xml:lang="en">The definition of organic compound is based on the IUPAC Gold Book. However, sometimes an organic compound is defined as a chemical compound that contains a carbon–hydrogen or carbon–carbon bond. Also, some carbon-containing compounds are typically not classified as organic, like carbides, carbonates, and cyanides.</emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f>
