  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_4207e895_8b83_4318_996a_72cfb32acd94">
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo/disciplines/materials#"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Material</skos:prefLabel>
    <emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f xml:lang="en">A instance of a material (e.g. nitrogen) can represent any state of matter. The fact that the individual also belongs to other classes (e.g. Gas) would reveal the actual form in which the material is found.</emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f>
    <emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f xml:lang="en">Material usually means some definite kind, quality, or quantity of matter, especially as intended for use.</emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f>
    <emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f xml:lang="en">A material may be either a mesoscopic or a continuum substance.</emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f>
    <emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">The class of individuals standing for an amount of ordinary matter substance.</emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The class of individuals standing for an amount of ordinary matter substance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Material</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
