    <emmo:EMMO_1f1b164d_ec6a_4faa_8d5e_88bda62316cc rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/ARCSEC</emmo:EMMO_1f1b164d_ec6a_4faa_8d5e_88bda62316cc>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">"Arc Second" is a unit of angular measure, also called the `second of arc`, equal to 1/60 arcminute. One arcsecond is a very small angle: there are 1,296,000 in a circle. The SI recommends `double prime` ('') as the symbol for the arcsecond. The symbol has become common in astronomy, where very small angles are stated in milliarcseconds (mas).

-- QUDT</rdfs:comment>
    <schema:unitCode rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">D62</schema:unitCode>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">SecondOfArc</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">ArcSecond</skos:altLabel>
    <emmo:EMMO_7f1dec83_d85e_4e1b_b7bd_c9442d4f5a64 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">\"</emmo:EMMO_7f1dec83_d85e_4e1b_b7bd_c9442d4f5a64>
