    <emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Process consisting of two steps: - first, the steel is heated in a quenching treatment to a temperature above Ac3 and then rapidly cooled in a liquid to produce a process-specific grain structure; - subsequently, the steel is heated to a specific temperature during tempering to set the desired property and cooled in air.</emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f>
