    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_4dbe2b16_3e84_4049_898d_eb89bcc925a2"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">`Coulomb Per Kilogram (C/kg)` is the unit in the category of Exposure. It is also known as coulombs per kilogram, coulomb/kilogram. This unit is commonly used in the SI unit system. Coulomb Per Kilogram (C/kg) has a dimension of M⁻¹TI where M is mass, T is time, and I is electric current. This unit is the standard SI unit in this category.

-- QUDT</rdfs:comment>
