    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A relation that identify a proper item part of the whole, whose parts always cover the full spatial extension of the whole within a time interval.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">hasTemporalPart</rdfs:label>
    <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_f722a7a9_864d_4896_a331_f90141f90a0a"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">hasTemporalPart</skos:prefLabel>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_55354438_7000_4284_b1b9_59d60c2261b9"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_22c91e99_61f8_4433_8853_432d44a2a46a"/>
    <emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f xml:lang="en">A temporal part of an item cannot both cause and be caused by any other proper part of the item.
A temporal part is not constraint to be causally self-connected, i.e. it can be either an item or a collection. We therefore introduce two subproperties in order to distinguish between both cases.</emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f>
    <emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f xml:lang="en">In EMMO FOL this is a defined property. In OWL temporal relations are primitive.</emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_c5ddfdba_c074_4aa4_ad6b_1ac4942d300d"/>
    <emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">A relation that identify a proper item part of the whole, whose parts always cover the full spatial extension of the whole within a time interval.</emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
  </rdf:Description>
