  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/emmo#Ampere">
    <emmo:EMMO_6dd685dd_1895_46e4_b227_be9f7d643c25 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">http://dbpedia.org/resource/Ampere</emmo:EMMO_6dd685dd_1895_46e4_b227_be9f7d643c25>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The ampere, symbol A, is the SI unit of electric current. It is defined by taking the fixed numerical value of the elementary charge e to be 1.602176634×10−19 when expressed in the unit C, which is equal to A s, where the second is defined in terms of ∆νCs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Ampere</rdfs:label>
    <emmo:EMMO_70fe84ff_99b6_4206_a9fc_9a8931836d84 xml:lang="en">The ampere, symbol A, is the SI unit of electric current. It is defined by taking the fixed numerical value of the elementary charge e to be 1.602176634×10−19 when expressed in the unit C, which is equal to A s, where the second is defined in terms of ∆νCs.</emmo:EMMO_70fe84ff_99b6_4206_a9fc_9a8931836d84>
