    <schema:unitCode rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">KGM</schema:unitCode>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The kilogram, symbol kg, is the SI unit of mass. It is defined by taking the fixed numerical value of the Planck constant h to be 6.62607015×10−34 when expressed in the unit J s, which is equal to kg m2 s−1, where the metre and the second are defined in terms of c and ∆νCs.</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Kilogram</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Kilogram</skos:altLabel>
    <emmo:EMMO_c84c6752_6d64_48cc_9500_e54a3c34898d rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kilogram?oldid=493633626</emmo:EMMO_c84c6752_6d64_48cc_9500_e54a3c34898d>
    <emmo:EMMO_70fe84ff_99b6_4206_a9fc_9a8931836d84 xml:lang="en">The kilogram, symbol kg, is the SI unit of mass. It is defined by taking the fixed numerical value of the Planck constant h to be 6.62607015×10−34 when expressed in the unit J s, which is equal to kg m2 s−1, where the metre and the second are defined in terms of c and ∆νCs.</emmo:EMMO_70fe84ff_99b6_4206_a9fc_9a8931836d84>
    <emmo:EMMO_6dd685dd_1895_46e4_b227_be9f7d643c25 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">http://dbpedia.org/resource/Kilogram</emmo:EMMO_6dd685dd_1895_46e4_b227_be9f7d643c25>
