    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Product of the ion activities of the ions resulting from the dissociation of a solute in a saturated solution, raised to powers equal to their stoichiometric numbers.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">For the dissociation of a salt AmBn → mA + nB, the solubility product is KSP = am(A) ⋅ an(B), where a is ionic activity and m and n are the stoichiometric numbers.</rdfs:comment>
