    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phot</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A phot (ph) is a photometric unit of illuminance, or luminous flux through an area. It is not an SI unit, but rather is associated with the older centimetre gram second system of units.  Metric dimensions: illuminance = luminous intensity × solid angle / length.

-- QUDT</rdfs:comment>
    <emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">A phot (ph) is a photometric unit of illuminance, or luminous flux through an area. It is not an SI unit, but rather is associated with the older centimetre gram second system of units.  Metric dimensions: illuminance = luminous intensity × solid angle / length.

-- QUDT</emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Phot</skos:prefLabel>
