    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://www.efunda.com/glossary/units/units--electric_current--statampere.cfm</rdfs:seeAlso>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo/disciplines/units/unclassifiedunits#"/>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/2.1/vocab/unit</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
    <emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">"Statampere" (statA) is a unit in the category of Electric current. It is also known as statamperes. This unit is commonly used in the cgs unit system. Statampere (statA) has a dimension of I where I is electric current. It can be converted to the corresponding standard SI unit A by multiplying its value by a factor of 3.355641E-010.

-- QUDT</emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">"Statampere" (statA) is a unit in the category of Electric current. It is also known as statamperes. This unit is commonly used in the cgs unit system. Statampere (statA) has a dimension of I where I is electric current. It can be converted to the corresponding standard SI unit A by multiplying its value by a factor of 3.355641E-010.

-- QUDT</rdfs:comment>
    <emmo:EMMO_1f1b164d_ec6a_4faa_8d5e_88bda62316cc rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/A_Stat</emmo:EMMO_1f1b164d_ec6a_4faa_8d5e_88bda62316cc>
