  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_8d2d9374_ef3a_47e6_8595_6bc208e07519">
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Theory</skos:prefLabel>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The 'theory' is e.g. a proposition, a book or a paper whose sub-symbols suggest in the mind of the interpreter an interpretant structure that can represent a 'physical'.

It is not an 'icon' (like a math equation), because it has no common resemblance or logical structure with the 'physical'.

In Peirce semiotics: legisign-symbol-argument</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A 'conventional' that stand for a 'physical'.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo/disciplines/models#"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
