    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">While a task is only an holistic part of a workflow, a task tile provide a more precise context about the placement of a task in the topological structure of a workflow by using a reductionistic categorization. A workflow is now seen as a tiling and the task is on of its tiles.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A task that is a well formed tile of a workflow, according to a reductionistic description.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">TaskTile</rdfs:label>
    <emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f xml:lang="en">A task tile is part of a specific granularity level for the workflow description, as composition of tasks.</emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f>
    <emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">A task that is a well formed tile of a workflow, according to a reductionistic description.</emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
