  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/emmo#MilliArcsecond">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Milli ArcSecond</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">MilliArcsecond</skos:prefLabel>
    <emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">A minute of arc, arcminute, or minute arc (MOA), is a unit of angular measurement equal to one sixtieth (1/60) of one degree (circle/21,600), or π /10,800 radians. In turn, a second of arc or arcsecond is one sixtieth (1/60) of one minute of arc. Since one degree is defined as one three hundred and sixtieth (1/360) of a rotation, one minute of arc is 1/21,600 of a rotation.  the milliarcsecond, abbreviated mas, is used in astronomy.

-- QUDT</emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
    <emmo:EMMO_1f1b164d_ec6a_4faa_8d5e_88bda62316cc rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliARCSEC</emmo:EMMO_1f1b164d_ec6a_4faa_8d5e_88bda62316cc>
