  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_d7788d1a_020d_4c78_85a1_13563fcec168">
    <emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f xml:lang="en">In Peirce semiotics three subtypes of icon are possible:
(a) the image, which depends on a simple quality (e.g. picture)
(b) the diagram, whose internal relations, mainly dyadic or so taken, represent by analogy the relations in something (e.g. math formula, geometric flowchart)
(c) the metaphor, which represents the representative character of a sign by representing a parallelism in something else
[Wikipedia]</emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f>
    <emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f xml:lang="en">If object and sign belongs to the same class, then the sign is fuctional, diagrammatic and resemblance.
For example, when a Boeing 747 is used as a sign for another Boeing 747.</emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Icon</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo/perspectives/semiotics#"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_4a2bf359_c47b_4aa3_9811_b59c3e1dac1e"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="n6a0b4d77db1d4bb4a28be148935c0b69b4708"/>
    <skos:example xml:lang="en">A picture that reproduces the aspect of a person.</skos:example>
    <skos:example xml:lang="en">An equation that reproduces the logical connection of the properties of a physical entity.</skos:example>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Simulacrum</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Model</skos:altLabel>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A sign that stands for an object by resembling or imitating it, in shape, function or by sharing a similar logical structure.</rdfs:comment>
    <emmo:EMMO_8a137e9f_579c_4e28_baca_e8980eb0c3db rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">EquivalentTo: AnalogicalIcon or ResemblanceIcon or FunctionalIcon</emmo:EMMO_8a137e9f_579c_4e28_baca_e8980eb0c3db>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Icon</skos:prefLabel>
    <emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">A sign that stands for an object by resembling or imitating it, in shape, function or by sharing a similar logical structure.</emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_8159c26a_494b_4fa0_9959_10888f152298">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">AmountOfSubstance</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_194100e1_e11a_4b7c_bb5a_171655679fc8"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_1a4c1a97_88a7_4d8e_b2f9_2ca58e92dde4"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="n6a0b4d77db1d4bb4a28be148935c0b69b3783"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_a06e3d38_1aa8_4f45_89a8_722dbacfda24"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The number of elementary entities present.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">"In the name “amount of substance”, the word “substance” will typically be replaced by words to specify the substance concerned in any particular application, for example “amount of hydrogen chloride, HCl”, or “amount of benzene, C6H6 ”. It is important to give a precise definition of the entity involved (as emphasized in the definition of the mole); this should preferably be done by specifying the molecular chemical formula of the material involved. Although the word “amount” has a more general dictionary definition, the abbreviation of the full name “amount of substance” to “amount” may be used for brevity."

-- SI Brochure</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">AmountOfSubstance</skos:prefLabel>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">The number of elementary entities present.</emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
    <emmo:EMMO_fe015383_afb3_44a6_ae86_043628697aa2 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">https://doi.org/10.1351/goldbook.A00297</emmo:EMMO_fe015383_afb3_44a6_ae86_043628697aa2>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo/disciplines/isq#"/>
    <emmo:EMMO_1f1b164d_ec6a_4faa_8d5e_88bda62316cc rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/AmountOfSubstance</emmo:EMMO_1f1b164d_ec6a_4faa_8d5e_88bda62316cc>
